diff --git a/artifacts/codex-runs/cisco-4h-lab-run-report.md b/artifacts/codex-runs/cisco-4h-lab-run-report.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f4ff124058dcc378d0adbc73470dc7e743dca575
--- /dev/null
+++ b/artifacts/codex-runs/cisco-4h-lab-run-report.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Cisco 4h Lab Run Report
+
+## Baseline
+
+- Started at: 2026-06-05T19:51:51Z
+- Workspace: `/home/administrator/infra-config-portal`
+- Provider mode requested: `local-lab-readwrite`
+- Env file requested: `.env.local.real-lab`
+- Git status: dirty worktree, branch `main` ahead of `origin/main` by 2 commits.
+- Safety note: secret values from `.env.local.real-lab` are not printed or stored in this report.
+
+## Stage 1 Baseline Findings
+
+- Existing Cisco readiness code is present in:
+  - `app/backend/app/providers/cisco_console.py`
+  - `app/backend/app/providers/cisco_ansible.py`
+  - `app/backend/app/services/cisco_setup_readiness.py`
+  - `app/backend/app/services/cisco_console_bootstrap.py`
+  - `app/backend/scripts/cisco_console_ethernet_readiness.py`
+- Existing bootstrap service is a guarded scaffold: it previews commands, but records `execution_supported=false` and blocks serial writes.
+- Existing readiness run completed with status `blocked`.
+- Existing readiness selected `/dev/serial/by-id/usb-Prolific_Technology_Inc._USB-Serial_Controller_D-if00-port0`.
+- Existing prompt readiness opened the port but captured no prompt text.
